<!-- Exercise 032 - UserControlComposition (beginner).
     Goal:   Nest two instances of the given Ex032_Badge UserControl and set
             each one's plain CLR Caption property to a distinct literal.
     Drills: nesting a UserControl, exposing a CLR property.
     Passes: dotnet test, filtered to Ex032_ (see the exact command in
     Ex032_UserControlComposition.axaml.cs - an XML comment may not hold two
     hyphens in a row, so it cannot appear here). -->
<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:b="clr-namespace:FeWoLearning.Avalonia.Exercises.Beginner"
             x:Class="FeWoLearning.Avalonia.Exercises.Beginner.Ex032_UserControlComposition">
  <!-- TODO: replace this placeholder with:
         <StackPanel Spacing="8">
           <b:Ex032_Badge Name="FirstBadge" Caption="Alpha" />
           <b:Ex032_Badge Name="SecondBadge" Caption="Beta" />
         </StackPanel>
       Ex032_Badge (given, do not change) exposes Caption as a plain CLR
       property - setting it here from XAML is an ordinary reflection-based
       property assignment, not a binding or a Style, because Caption is not
       an AvaloniaProperty. Two plain TextBlocks reading "Alpha"/"Beta"
       reproduce the same rendered text with no Badge nested at all - the
       test looks for two actual Ex032_Badge instances in the tree before it
       ever reads their text. -->
  <StackPanel>
    <TextBlock Text="TODO" />
  </StackPanel>
</UserControl>
